# Signing — NEVER commit these
*.pem
content-signing-key*

# PHASE C — SIGNED ARTEFACTS ARE BUILD OUTPUT, NOT SOURCE.
#
# manifest.json, manifest.sig and index.sig are all derived from content plus a
# private key. Committing them means the repo carries signatures that go stale
# the moment anyone edits the content beside them, and a stale signature in git
# is worse than none: it looks authoritative, verifies against nothing, and the
# next person assumes the content is what was signed.
#
# The signing step regenerates them into backend/dist/ on every publish. The
# only thing that belongs in git is the authored content and the PUBLIC key.
backend/dist/
backend/content/**/manifest.json
backend/content/**/manifest.sig
backend/content/**/index.sig

# The private signing key must never come near this repo.
*.key
*pack-signing*
mindberzerk-3eaf5-firebase-adminsdk-fbsvc-388e9a4d01.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.jsonfirebase-debug.log
# ── iconlab ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Downloaded icon themes and everything derived from them. Hundreds of
# megabytes of other people's GPL artwork, kept locally as drawing reference
# and deliberately never committed: it does not belong in this repo's history,
# and nothing here is used at build or publish time.
#
# `tools/iconlab.mjs` recreates `matches/` and `index.html` from `sources/` on
# every run, so the only thing that would ever be worth keeping is the sources,
# and those came from the internet.
iconlab/
